  "sport": "floorball",
  "title": "Corner duel – getting out of the corner",
  "description": "A 1v1 duel in a corner of the rink. Place a cone about one metre out from the boards on each side of the corner – those are the two exits. The players line up between the exits, facing the corner: attackers (blue) and defenders (red).\n\nThe coach plays the ball into the corner. The first attacker starts one step ahead of the first defender. The attacker has to get out with the ball through either exit, between the cone and the boards. The defender has to stop that and win the ball back as quickly as possible. Afterwards, join the back of the other line. The diagram is not to scale – the corner is drawn bigger.",
  "coachingPoints": [
    {
      "id": "cp1",
      "text": "Attack: shield the ball with your body against the boards and look for the exit the defender leaves open."
    },
    {
      "id": "cp2",
      "text": "Attack: fake towards one exit and go for the other."
    },
    {
      "id": "cp3",
      "text": "Defence: close the nearest exit and force the attacker into the corner."
    },
    {
      "id": "cp4",
      "text": "Ask the players: what is the best way to defend – and what can you try as an attacker?"
    }
  ],
  "locale": "en",
